{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31825 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Jerantinine B exerts its biological activity by targeting the mitochondrial Thioredoxin, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver, Isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside, and Uvaol-3-Caffeate. All these compounds ultimately interact with the CD276 antigen, indicating a potential pathway where Jerantinine B may influence CD276 through its interaction with Thioredoxin. The shared targeting of Thioredoxin by different compounds supports the idea that this molecule plays a central role in the mechanism of action of Jerantinine B. The evidence suggests that the interaction between Jerantinine B and CD276 may involve a downstream pathway where Thioredoxin acts as a mediator, possibly through a common cellular target or a shared signaling mechanism. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the integrated evidence points to a plausible, albeit indirect, relationship between Jerantinine B and CD276 via the Thioredoxin pathway.",
